43d999f53d8749dd0b33fe897d09f8f23a6151e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-46452" :question/id #uuid "34184e66-1d20-589f-98d3-e6700006273c" :question/math-academy-id "q-46452" :question/problem "Factor $2{y}^{2}-8y+26.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(y)=2{y}^{2}-8y+26.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(y)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-8y+26 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y+13 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot y+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}+13 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4+13 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & ={(3\\text{i})}^{2} \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ y & =2\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ the expression $2{y}^{2}-8y+26$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-8y+26 & =a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-46452/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-46452"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-46588/selection/45d306b7ea320d54762dc2c608d2e117b97dfcb5d503bcafe87e31c51c25cd82" :answer/id #uuid "56ad7dde-8db0-5afb-9f99-61bb479a2dd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-24y+27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-46588/selection/f9de20b687ae38a9e231438acdd1d532df7d91a2a54c4ac04ecfaa09b4be7ec0" :answer/id #uuid "6ade4beb-68f9-5374-9c02-810b957b08db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-9y+27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-46588/selection/acf45addca9e292229cc16c8c2fb0da38452b24d88298ce858fdd8bfc373a657" :answer/id #uuid "42632239-8018-56ee-907e-78d2d1fe1b1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :a